{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact D6 head 881f703550b52d8979baa771c10551423a46d2f5 on builder/security-docs-d6-20261109, tree cbd07900, all ten artifacts, for request d8512f74 under promise 40f21bcc and review request aa828cc0. The head adds SECURITY.md and D6, the security invariants page. It also adds a static check that D6's nine named tests exist, and it corrects D4's deployment references. No production source, setting, binding, pin or seal changes.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- D6 states each of the five invariants with its limit. `verified-genesis` keeps the R2 residual that ruling 2c18d9be accepted: a refused native creation can leave unregistered storage. `session-membership` keeps the issued-session window, and `credential-custody` keeps the provider lifetime. D6 says that R3 is still queued and that current code can fetch foreign facts and drain timed work before a grant refusal. Nothing on the page claims more than the code does.\n- The witnesses. I ran `node scripts/security-witnesses.mjs` read-only at the head: 9 witnesses, 5 invariants, 8 files. The checker parses each tracked test file with rolldown's parseAst and counts only literal `test` or `it` calls with a function callback. Each row must match exactly one declaration. Paths must be tracked `.test.ts` or `.test.mjs` files under packages or apps, with no `.` or `..` segment. The new Node case renames the first witness and leaves the old name only in a comment, then requires the check to fail. The page says that this check proves existence only, not assertion meaning or a passing result.\n- D4 against the checked-in configs:\n  - apps/room/wrangler.jsonc is the neutral template: enforce mode, namespace `dap-self-host`, empty screen hosts, no bucket, dataset or register.\n  - wrangler.connect.jsonc sets `DEPLOYMENT` dap-connect, enforce mode, the `PLANNED_O4_REGISTER_SCOPE` placeholder, `MCP_ENABLED` \"false\", empty screen hosts, the bucket `dap-connect-application-content` and the cohort register@27, directory@26, membership@13, rules@10, destination@20, inbox@1.\n  - Exactly four configs name `artroom_metrics_v1`: artroom-scope, grow, demo and commons.\n  - packages/client/src/creation-offer.ts accepts register@17 and register@26, which matches \"Registers 17 and 26\".\n- SECURITY.md gives the private GitHub reporting path, links D1 through D6, and marks the 4 October review as historical. The review file gains a three-line status header.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main ca6a54e2 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the ten paths that its ten artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 8 checked, 0 flagged. Between gate 2 at a199a9ef and the head, only the note and the gate 2 manifest change.\n- The gates. I read gate.exit for gate 1 at bf5d64fb, tree 26c0ddde: \"exit 2\", at the whitespace stage, with every test unreached. It stays failed. I read gate.exit for gate 2 at a199a9ef, tree 94bf396a, which ruling a47f6290 authorized: \"exit 0\". The unchanged selector omits Scale, and the note says so.\n- The evidence. The three manifests hash to the values that the note cites: 979d191b, a0ff9f77 and 69710f07. Their 58 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The witness inventory lives in the document as one fenced JSON block, and a Node owner that already runs checks it. No second copy of any runtime test exists.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The page qualifies every invariant and names R2's accepted residual, the issued-session window, the cross-scope cache window, the shared resources and the queued R3 order.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nNo deployment is needed. This approval closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:16ef5eff7823615cdae1f2c3c9588d11832d8282","binding":"assigned","head":"881f703550b52d8979baa771c105514